WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.290
I'm Jenna Fisher, and I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是珍娜·费舍尔，我是安吉拉·金赛。

2
00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.150
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

3
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:13.270
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你们制作了这个终极《办公室》粉丝播客。

4
00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:17.790
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

5
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.970
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
分享幕后细节，还有许多我们闺蜜之间的故事。

6
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.010
We're The Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士》6.0版。

7
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.400
Ooh, hi there.
噢，嗨。

8
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:26.920
Hi.
嗨。

9
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.840
Ooh, we have some special guests today.
噢，今天我们有几位特别嘉宾。

10
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.660
We do.
没错。

11
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.880
This is the most we've ever talked on the podcast as a group.
这是我们在播客里人数最多的一次谈话了。

12
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.180
You've never had five people?
你们从来没请过五个人吗？

13
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:35.580
No.
没有。

14
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:36.080
Correct.
没错。

15
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.520
Angela, do you want to tell everybody what's happening?
安吉拉，你想告诉大家发生了什么吗？

16
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.280
I sure do.
我当然想。

17
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.160
We have a super fun episode today because we are doing a crossover with Pod Meets World.
今天这期节目超级有趣，因为我们要和《Pod Meets World》进行联动。

18
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.000
We have Ryder Danielle and Will from Boy Meets World.
我们请来了《男孩成长记》的莱德、丹妮尔和威尔。

19
00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.020
We each got to watch an episode of each other's show.
我们每个人都看了对方节目的一集。

20
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:52.920
Yes.
是的。

21
00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:53.720
Yes.
是的。

22
00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.480
Okay, Jenna, why don't you share with everyone how this episode came about?
好的，珍娜，你来跟大家分享一下这期节目是怎么促成的吧？

23
00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.220
Okay, well, Ryder and I know each other.
好的，其实莱德和我认识。

24
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:00.600
Yeah.
没错。

25
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.780
That's how this came about.
这就是促成这次合作的原因。

26
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.460
How do you guys know each other?
你们是怎么认识的？

27
00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:03.640
Yes.
是的。

28
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.940
We have a mutual friend in Natalie Z.
我们有一位共同的朋友，娜塔莉·Z。

29
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.520
Party's at their house, right?
是在他们家聚会认识的，对吧？

30
00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:08.760
How far do you guys go back?
你们认识多久了？

31
00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.880
So, Travis Schult is friends with my husband, Lee.
特拉维斯·舒尔特和我丈夫李是朋友。

32
00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:12.760
Okay, so it's Travis.
好的，所以是特拉维斯。

33
00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:13.680
Okay, okay.
好的，好的。

34
00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.300
Travis, who is married to Natalie.
特拉维斯，他娶了娜塔莉。

35
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.780
Travis and Natalie will have a party here and there, and you're there, and I'm there.
特拉维斯和娜塔莉偶尔会举办聚会，你会在那儿，我也会在那儿。

36
00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:20.080
Yeah.
没错。

37
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.420
One of the first people I talked to about Pod Meets World when I was back because I was
当我回来时，我是最早和你们聊《Pod Meets World》的人之一，因为我当时在想，

38
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.400
like, how's your rewatch podcast going?
你们的重温播客做得怎么样了？

39
00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.700
And you were super helpful and you were like, do it.
你当时特别热心，你说，做吧。

40
00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:28.840
You'll have the best time.
你会玩得很开心的。

41
00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:29.680
It's so good.
这真的太棒了。

42
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.660
And yeah, you were like one of the people that really convinced me that this was a great idea.
没错，你就是那些真正说服我这是一个好主意的人之一。

43
00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:34.620
Oh, good.
噢，太好了。

44
00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:35.440
Oh, I'm so glad.
噢，我真高兴。

45
00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.380
Well, your podcast is super successful.
你们的播客非常成功。

46
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.900
You guys have an amazing community.
你们拥有一个很棒的社区。

47
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.400
You guys are real friends in real life, like me and Angela.
你们在现实生活中也是真正的朋友，就像我和安吉拉一样。

48
00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:44.100
Yes.
是的。

49
00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.360
You do a fantastic job telling the show, telling all the scenes and what goes on behind.
你们在讲述节目、讲述所有场景以及幕后故事方面做得非常出色。

50
00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.120
I think it's just such a great podcaSt.
我觉得这真是一个很棒的播客。

51
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:51.680
Thank you.
谢谢。

52
00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.160
And I really am so curious to watch more episodes now.
而且我现在真的非常好奇，想看更多的剧集。

53
00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:56.400
Truly, truly.
真的，真的。

54
00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.060
Especially now that I know some of the things you shared with us.
尤其是现在我知道了你和我们分享的一些事情之后。

55
00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:00.560
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

56
00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.600
For a little trivia.
作为一点小花絮。

57
00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.060
How did we get there?
我们是怎么聊到这儿的？

58
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:03.320
Yeah.
是啊。

59
00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.200
Yes, yes.
没错，没错。

60
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.520
Because full disclosure, Angela and I had not seen an episode of Boy Meets World
因为坦白说，安吉拉和我之前从来没看过一集《男孩看世界》

61
00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.420
until this collab happened.
直到这次合作发生。

62
00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.460
I think similarly, Ryder, had you ever seen an episode of The Office?
我想问问赖德，你以前看过《办公室》吗？

63
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.620
Yeah, I'd only watched probably the first two seasons, maybe, or maybe up to three.
看过，我大概只看了前两季，或者可能到第三季吧。

64
00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:21.340
So you had not seen the episode we picked for today then?
所以你还没看过我们今天选的那一集？

65
00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:21.620
No, no.
没，没看过。

66
00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:27.160
Will has seen every episode of The Office numerous times.
威尔已经把《办公室》的每一集都看了无数遍了。

67
00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:27.680
Yes.
是的。

68
00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.900
I'm also a little weird when it comes to TV.
我在看电视这方面也有点怪。

69
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.680
So if I see it more than once, I can recite it backwards and forwards.
如果我看过一遍以上，我就能倒背如流。

70
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:37.520
So I watched the episode again, you had us watch, but I didn't need to.
所以我又看了一遍你们让我看的那一集，但其实我根本不需要看。

71
00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.440
I could have literally told you what you were wearing, usually, in most of the seasons.
我甚至能直接告诉你，在大多数季里，你穿的是什么衣服。

72
00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:40.980
Wow.
哇。

73
00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.100
He knew it very well.
他确实非常了解。

74
00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.460
You're like a genius person?
你就像个天才一样？

75
00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:43.880
Yes.
是的。

76
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:44.480
With TV.
在电视方面。

77
00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:45.380
Photographic memory?
过目不忘？

78
00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:45.620
Yeah.
是啊。

79
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:45.900
TV.
电视方面。

80
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:46.280
Wow.
哇。

81
00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.100
Yeah, with TV.
是啊，在电视方面。

82
00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.340
So if I have nothing to do and I'm bored and there's nothing around me, I shut my eyes
所以如果我没事做，感到无聊，周围又没别的事，我就闭上眼睛

83
00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.000
and watch MASH.
在脑子里看《陆军野战医院》。

84
00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:52.780
Come on.
得了吧。

85
00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.280
It's true.
是真的。

86
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.040
Backwards, forwards.
倒着看，顺着看。

87
00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.700
Because you can just play that in your head.
因为你可以在脑子里直接播放。

88
00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.200
Yeah, so I can do that with The Office, too.
是啊，所以我看《办公室》也能做到这一点。

89
00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.640
And the images are there, as well as the...
画面都在那儿，还有……

90
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.060
The images, the sound, the music, the breaks, all of it's in.
画面、声音、音乐、停顿，所有的一切都在里面。

91
00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:05.360
And what if he doesn't have his giant calendar in front of him?
那如果他面前没有那个巨大的日历呢？

92
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:05.700
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

93
00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:06.480
He can't remember...
他就记不住……

94
00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.900
He can't remember what there is to do or whether or not something is scheduled, so...
他记不住有什么事要做，或者有没有安排什么日程，所以……

95
00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:13.920
My wife helps, but no, I don't.
我妻子会帮忙，但确实，我自己记不住。

96
00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:14.900
Yeah, no, so it's...
是啊，所以就是……

97
00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:15.300
But TV.
但电视方面没问题。

98
00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:16.300
Selective genius.
选择性天才。

99
00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:17.060
Backwards and forwards.
倒背如流。

100
00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.860
There's a little bit of undercurrent business happening in this conversation.
这段对话里似乎暗藏玄机。

101
00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.000
You know, they just know not to ask anymore.
你知道，他们只是知道别再问了。

102
00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:24.540
Oh, no.
噢，不。

103
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.900
Be here at such and such a time, and she'll text my wife.
比如几点几分到那儿，她就会发短信给我妻子。

104
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.200
We also just say, could you just take a picture of the big calendar?
我们也会说，你能不能直接拍张大日历的照片？

105
00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:29.540
Yeah.
是啊。

106
00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.640
Because I understand that you can't care.
因为我理解你没法操心这些。

107
00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.720
It's a literal giant calendar.
那真的是个巨大的日历。

108
00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.040
Right.
对。

109
00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.000
So I'll say, because if you just had the picture of it, you'd know if you were free on the 8th.
所以我就会说，因为如果你有照片，你就能知道8号那天你有没有空。

110
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.300
This is a really good idea.
这主意真不错。

111
00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.520
So did you take a picture of your calendar?
那你拍你的日历了吗？

112
00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.440
I think the last one I took was in April.
我想我最后一次拍是在四月。

113
00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:43.020
Yeah.
是啊。

114
00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.340
So I have through April.
所以我只知道四月之前的情况。

115
00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:45.080
Okay.
好吧。

116
00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:46.060
Where I'm supposed to be.
我该去哪儿。

117
00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:46.500
You know what?
你知道吗？

118
00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.360
Otherwise, they just tell me where I'm supposed to be most of the time.
不然的话，他们大部分时间只会直接告诉我该去哪儿。

119
00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.120
You guys, we are actually in your studio today.
各位，我们今天真的在你们的工作室里。

120
00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.920
It's lovely, and there are cameras.
这里很棒，还有摄像机。

121
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.920
I feel like they could make a video for you of your calendar that you would watch, and
我觉得他们可以为你拍一段你日历的视频，你可以看看，然后

122
00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.180
then you would know everything.
你就什么都知道了。

123
00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:00.320
That's not a bad idea.
这主意不错。

124
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.420
I'd know where I'd have to be and all the stuff I had to do.
我就能知道我得去哪儿，还有我得做些什么。

125
00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.540
Again, comes to episodes of The Office all day long.
再说一次，整天都在看《办公室》的剧集。

126
00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.760
Where I have to be tomorrow, anybody's guess.
明天我得去哪儿，谁也猜不到。

127
00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:07.940
No idea.
完全不知道。

128
00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.280
I feel like you could be a really good asset for Office ladies.
我觉得你可以成为《办公室女士》的一大助力。

129
00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.600
What would you like to know?
你想知道些什么？

130
00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:15.420
I mean, we're going to hit you up.
我是说，我们会找你帮忙的。

131
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:15.880
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

132
00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:16.720
Yeah.
好。

133
00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:17.840
Please, let me know.
请务必告诉我。

134
00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.520
Be happy to.
我很乐意。

135
00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:19.440
I'll walk you through it.
我会带你了解一下。

136
00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:19.980
It's a great show.
那是个很棒的节目。

137
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:20.740
Oh, thank you.
噢，谢谢你。

138
00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.200
Not to belabor this, but I am really fascinated.
不是想纠结这个问题，但我真的很着迷。

139
00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.940
Does this extend as well to things you've read, books, articles?
这是否也适用于你读过的东西，比如书、文章？

140
00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.800
It depends on what, if it's stuck in my brain, it's forever stuck in my brain, and I can go
这取决于是什么，如果它印在我的脑海里，它就永远印在我的脑海里，我可以回想

141
00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.400
back and see the page, see the thing.
并看到那一页，看到那个内容。

142
00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.100
But then again, a calculea is a very real thing.
但话又说回来，计算障碍是真实存在的。

143
00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.980
So put two numbers in front of me, and my brain doesn't comprehend it.
所以把两个数字放在我面前，我的大脑就无法理解。

144
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.720
You also, in school, wouldn't take notes.
你在学校时也不记笔记。

145
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.980
You would just watch the teacher.
你只是看着老师。

146
00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:43.360
I could.
我可以。

147
00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.660
Because if I looked down and take notes.
因为如果我低头记笔记的话。

148
00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:45.420
If you looked down, you wouldn't.
如果你低头，你就记不住了。

149
00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.180
But if he just listened.
但如果他只是听着。

150
00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.240
If I listened and just watched the board, then I could just see the board.
如果我听着并看着黑板，我就能直接看到黑板上的内容。

151
00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:49.560
Right.
没错。

152
00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:52.120
No, but again, somebody gave me a phone number or people's names.
不，但话说回来，有人给了我一个电话号码或者别人的名字。

153
00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:55.180
I have to meet somebody a thousand times before I remember their names.
我得见一个人一千次才能记住他们的名字。

154
00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.800
But I can see the blue shirt you're wearing.
但我能看见你穿的那件蓝色衬衫。

155
00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:01.880
I can see the shirt you walk in on when fashion show, fashion show at lunch.
我能看见你走秀时穿的那件衬衫，午餐时的时装秀。

156
00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.520
I can see the color of the few shows.
我能看见那几场秀的颜色。

157
00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.160
You guys should quiz him.
你们应该考考他。

158
00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:04.780
You should ask him.
你们应该问问他。

159
00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.760
If you remember a certain line or a moment.
如果你记得某句台词或某个瞬间的话。

160
00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.960
Yeah, so stuff like that.
是啊，就是诸如此类的事。

161
00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:11.760
It's so crazy because we just did a side-by-side.
太疯狂了，因为我们刚才做了个对比图。

162
00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:18.340
A fan wrote in and said that they think that Josh in Stamford is wearing the same suit that
有粉丝写信说，他们觉得斯坦福分部的乔什穿的那套西装和

163
00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.320
Michael Scott wears on his birthday.
迈克尔·斯科特生日那天穿的是同一套。

164
