我记得看过你们剪辑师的采访，他说当他在剪辑

1165
00:38:07.280 --> 00:38:12.000
scene where Jim and Pam are on the boat for the booze cruise that he's editing, he goes,
吉姆和帕姆在游船派对上的那场戏时，他一边剪一边说，

1166
00:38:12.140 --> 00:38:13.500
I knew what happened.
我知道接下来会发生什么。

1167
00:38:13.500 --> 00:38:15.480
And I was still there going, kiss her.
但我还是忍不住在那儿喊：亲她。

1168
00:38:15.680 --> 00:38:16.340
Kiss her.
亲她。

1169
00:38:16.520 --> 00:38:17.340
Come on, Jim.
加油，吉姆。

1170
00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:17.860
Kiss her.
亲她。

1171
00:38:17.940 --> 00:38:19.340
You're working on the show.
你明明是在参与制作这部剧。

1172
00:38:19.440 --> 00:38:20.920
You know what's going to happen.
你知道剧情走向。

1173
00:38:20.920 --> 00:38:24.880
And you're still so invested that you're yelling at the screen to have the characters kiss.
但你依然如此投入，甚至对着屏幕大喊，希望角色们能亲吻。

1174
00:38:24.880 --> 00:38:29.840
That's rare in any medium, but on television at the time, it was unheard of.
这在任何媒介中都很少见，而在当时的电视界，这简直是闻所未闻。

1175
00:38:30.020 --> 00:38:33.040
So we were yelling at the screen, things like that.
所以我们当时对着屏幕大喊，诸如此类的话。

1176
00:38:33.160 --> 00:38:33.540
Kiss her.
亲她。

1177
00:38:33.680 --> 00:38:34.300
And oh, my God.
天哪。

1178
00:38:34.520 --> 00:38:36.880
And Jim can't come back from Stanford with her.
吉姆不能就这么和她一起从斯坦福回来。

1179
00:38:37.080 --> 00:38:37.320
Come on.
拜托。

1180
00:38:37.600 --> 00:38:38.420
And Pam's doing this.
帕姆当时在做这个。

1181
00:38:38.520 --> 00:38:41.100
When she walks across the hot coals, we were just invested in everything.
当她走过滚烫的煤炭时，我们对一切都全身心投入。

1182
00:38:41.380 --> 00:38:43.660
And then on top of that, it was hysterical.
而且除此之外，它还非常搞笑。

1183
00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:47.320
So that was just an added bonus to the show was lightning in a bottle.
所以这只是额外的加分项，这部剧简直是可遇不可求的杰作。

1184
00:38:47.460 --> 00:38:49.560
I mean, it's tough to get that again.
我是说，很难再重现那样的辉煌了。

1185
00:38:49.560 --> 00:38:50.940
I don't know if we ever will, frankly.
坦白说，我不知道我们是否还能做到。

1186
00:38:50.940 --> 00:38:55.700
I mean, I don't know if I ever will, you know, it was it was a dream job.
我是说，我不知道我是否还能遇到，你知道，那是一份梦寐以求的工作。

1187
00:38:55.900 --> 00:38:58.480
They came around at the exact right time.
它出现的时机恰到好处。

1188
00:38:58.880 --> 00:39:00.500
And I felt like I was ready.
而且我觉得自己准备好了。

1189
00:39:00.900 --> 00:39:06.760
My acting coach always says successful come when your readiness meets the opportunities.
我的表演教练常说，成功源于准备与机遇的碰撞。

1190
00:39:06.940 --> 00:39:11.180
And so you can be as ready as you are and then never have an opportunity.
你可以准备得非常充分，却永远等不到机会。

1191
00:39:11.360 --> 00:39:13.800
But likewise, you can have all the opportunities in the world,
同样地，你也可以拥有全世界所有的机会，

1192
00:39:13.980 --> 00:39:17.120
which I was getting with all of my auditions for three camera shows.
就像我当时参加所有三机位情景喜剧试镜那样。

1193
00:39:17.160 --> 00:39:18.720
But I wasn't ready.
但我当时还没准备好。

1194
00:39:18.720 --> 00:39:24.460
And so the office for me was the thing where finally the opportunity met the readiness.
所以对我来说，《办公室》就是那个终于让机遇与准备相遇的项目。

1195
00:39:24.780 --> 00:39:26.760
I think that's true for a lot of our cast, too,
我想这对我们很多演员来说也是如此，

1196
00:39:26.880 --> 00:39:31.080
because we had a lot of really great seasoned comedians that had just been,
因为我们有很多非常出色的资深喜剧演员，他们之前一直

1197
00:39:31.080 --> 00:39:32.460
you know, plugging away.
你知道，在默默耕耘。

1198
00:39:32.680 --> 00:39:34.180
Kate Flannery is hilarious.
凯特·弗兰纳里非常搞笑。

1199
00:39:34.480 --> 00:39:37.740
She was part of a lounge act called The Lampshades.
她曾是一个叫“灯罩”的酒廊表演组合的成员。

1200
00:39:37.980 --> 00:39:39.900
Oscar Nunez, I had met at the Groundlings.
奥斯卡·努内兹，我是在“地基”喜剧团认识他的。

1201
00:39:40.040 --> 00:39:41.280
He was in Hot Towel.
他出演了《热毛巾》。

1202
00:39:42.260 --> 00:39:43.600
We had a scene together.
我们一起拍过一场戏。

1203
00:39:43.600 --> 00:39:47.620
You know, obviously, Steve, Rain, everyone had been sort of putting their dues in,
你知道，显然史蒂夫、雷恩，每个人都算是付出了努力，

1204
00:39:47.720 --> 00:39:49.840
putting their time in, and it was just that right moment.
投入了时间，而那正是恰逢其时的时刻。

1205
00:39:50.060 --> 00:39:51.460
But I have a question for you guys.
但我有个问题想问你们。

1206
00:39:51.860 --> 00:39:57.560
So, OK, if you could play a character on The Office, like, which one would you want to play?
那么，好吧，如果你们能在《办公室》里演一个角色，你们想演哪一个？

1207
00:39:57.720 --> 00:39:58.960
Oh, that's such a good question.
噢，这真是个好问题。

1208
00:39:59.380 --> 00:40:00.900
Will, I really hope you say Dwight.
威尔，我真希望你说的是德怀特。

1209
00:40:01.180 --> 00:40:02.120
Yeah, we've got to be Dwight.
没错，我们得演德怀特。

1210
00:40:02.120 --> 00:40:04.180
The comedy does actually tend itself towards Dwight.
这部剧的喜剧效果确实更偏向德怀特。

1211
00:40:04.300 --> 00:40:04.680
It does.
确实如此。

1212
00:40:04.900 --> 00:40:05.760
You'd be Jim.
你会是吉姆。

1213
00:40:05.900 --> 00:40:06.100
Yeah.
没错。

1214
00:40:07.020 --> 00:40:08.480
I'd be Dwight, and you'd be Pam.
我会是德怀特，而你会是帕姆。

1215
00:40:08.600 --> 00:40:09.360
I'd want to be Pam.
我想演帕姆。

1216
00:40:09.500 --> 00:40:11.120
Yeah, I would have to agree with that assessment.
是的，我不得不赞同这个评价。

1217
00:40:11.340 --> 00:40:11.540
Yeah.
没错。

1218
00:40:12.080 --> 00:40:13.980
I would have to agree with that assessment entirely.
我完全赞同这个评价。

1219
00:40:14.220 --> 00:40:18.180
Now, I really, really wish we had brought a Jim-Pam-Dwight scene with us.
现在，我真的、真的很希望我们带了一段吉姆、帕姆和德怀特的戏过来。

1220
00:40:18.420 --> 00:40:20.280
We should do that next time.
我们下次应该这么做。

1221
00:40:20.280 --> 00:40:21.120
Which scene would you like?
你们想演哪一场戏？

1222
00:40:24.260 --> 00:40:25.240
Which scene would you like?
你们想演哪一场戏？

1223
00:40:25.940 --> 00:40:29.360
No, I mean, that's definitely how I would have cast it, too,
不，我是说，如果非得是我们三个人来演的话，

1224
00:40:29.460 --> 00:40:31.340
if it had to be the three of us to do it.
那绝对也是我会选的角色分配。

1225
00:40:31.340 --> 00:40:32.380
It would have been that.
肯定会是那样。

1226
00:40:32.660 --> 00:40:33.060
So great.
太棒了。

1227
00:40:33.240 --> 00:40:36.380
Is it true that there was a chance you guys were going to be canceled after the first six?
你们在拍完前六集后差点被砍掉，这是真的吗？

1228
00:40:36.620 --> 00:40:37.240
Oh, yeah.
噢，是真的。

1229
00:40:37.440 --> 00:40:38.940
Not just after the first six.
不仅仅是在前六集之后。

1230
00:40:39.100 --> 00:40:42.740
The first six episodes, any day when we went, we were like, oh, we're still here.
前六集的时候，我们每天去片场都在想，噢，我们还在呢。

1231
00:40:42.860 --> 00:40:43.040
Yay.
耶。

1232
00:40:43.240 --> 00:40:43.820
It's crazy.
太疯狂了。

1233
00:40:43.940 --> 00:40:45.560
And we were not a hit.
而且我们当时并不火。

1234
00:40:45.900 --> 00:40:48.660
And also, NBC wasn't rallying behind us at all.
况且NBC根本没打算支持我们。

1235
00:40:48.700 --> 00:40:51.380
No, we were very surprised to get a pickup for season two,
没错，我们能拿到第二季的续订非常惊讶，

1236
00:40:51.520 --> 00:40:53.980
but the pickup for season two was only six episodes.
但第二季的续订只有六集。

1237
00:40:54.440 --> 00:40:55.020
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1238
00:40:55.700 --> 00:40:58.440
And then they ordered only six more.
然后他们又只续订了六集。

1239
00:40:58.840 --> 00:40:58.960
Yeah.
没错。

1240
00:40:58.960 --> 00:41:03.460
And then they ordered the back 12, and we ended up with 24 episodes.
后来他们续订了剩下的12集，我们最终拍了24集。

1241
00:41:03.620 --> 00:41:04.360
I mean, yeah.
我是说，确实。

1242
00:41:04.720 --> 00:41:08.600
At the end of this six episodes, those first six, they printed my name on paper,
在那六集结束时，也就是最初的那六集，他们把我的名字印在纸上，

1243
00:41:08.760 --> 00:41:12.140
and they just laminated it with some Velcro, and that's what was on my door.
然后用魔术贴把它塑封起来，那就是贴在我门上的东西。

1244
00:41:12.540 --> 00:41:15.560
So I took my laminated piece of paper home with me.
所以我把那张塑封的纸带回家了。

1245
00:41:15.960 --> 00:41:16.380
Yeah.
没错。

1246
00:41:17.900 --> 00:41:19.040
I'll save it forever.
我会永远珍藏它。

1247
00:41:19.600 --> 00:41:21.040
Because we just thought that was it.
因为我们当时觉得那就是终点了。

1248
00:41:21.280 --> 00:41:21.460
That was it.
那就是终点了。

1249
00:41:21.460 --> 00:41:26.940
So what episode would you then look to and say, that's the one where we knew what we were doing.
那么你们会觉得哪一集是你们意识到自己渐入佳境的转折点？

1250
00:41:27.080 --> 00:41:29.000
Everybody knew we were going to go from here.
大家都知道从那一刻起我们要起飞了。

1251
00:41:29.200 --> 00:41:30.020
We're now a hit.
我们现在火了。

1252
00:41:30.200 --> 00:41:30.960
This is what's going to happen.
接下来会发生这样的事。

1253
00:41:31.180 --> 00:41:37.500
It's very clear to me as far as like the downloads, because the Christmas episode with Yankee Swap
就下载量而言，我看得非常清楚，因为那集圣诞特辑，有白象交换礼物环节，

1254
00:41:37.500 --> 00:41:42.920
and Baby's playing jazz poster and Phyllis' sad oven mitt, all of that, the teapot,
还有宝贝演奏爵士乐的海报、菲利斯的悲惨烤箱手套，所有这些，还有那个茶壶，

1255
00:41:43.380 --> 00:41:45.940
that episode became the number one download on iTunes.
那一集成了iTunes上的下载量冠军。

1256
00:41:46.180 --> 00:41:46.480
Okay.
好的。

1257
00:41:46.920 --> 00:41:47.300
And so...
所以……

1258
00:41:47.780 --> 00:41:49.040
The ratings weren't there.
收视率当时并不高。

1259
00:41:49.180 --> 00:41:50.280
The ratings weren't there.
收视率当时并不高。

1260
00:41:50.600 --> 00:41:56.660
But this new world of like, oh, wait, we can make money off of this other thing,
但在这个新世界里，人们会想，哦，等等，我们可以通过其他方式赚钱，

1261
00:41:56.920 --> 00:41:58.620
this downloadable item.
比如这种可下载的内容。

1262
00:41:58.620 --> 00:41:59.700
Not the caSt.
演员们可没钱拿。

1263
00:41:59.900 --> 00:42:00.060
Right.
没错。

1264
00:42:00.220 --> 00:42:01.360
The cast doesn't get money for that.
演员们拿不到那部分的钱。

1265
00:42:01.460 --> 00:42:01.800
Right, right.
对，没错。

1266
00:42:01.980 --> 00:42:04.600
But people were watching it on their iPods, remember?
但人们当时是在iPod上看的，还记得吗？

1267
00:42:04.920 --> 00:42:05.440
Like, yes.
没错，是这样。

1268
00:42:05.840 --> 00:42:06.620
And they were like, okay.
他们当时觉得，好吧。

1269
00:42:06.620 --> 00:42:07.500
Also for the Yankee Swap.
白象交换礼物那集也是。

1270
00:42:07.580 --> 00:42:07.700
Yes.
是的。

1271
00:42:07.920 --> 00:42:08.340
There you go.
就是这样。

1272
00:42:08.460 --> 00:42:08.900
There you go.
就是这样。

1273
00:42:08.980 --> 00:42:09.460
Video iPod.
视频iPod。

1274
00:42:09.540 --> 00:42:10.660
Now, what about you guys?
那么，你们呢？

1275
00:42:10.860 --> 00:42:11.980
Did you always have...
你们一直都有……

1276
00:42:11.980 --> 00:42:15.700
Well, you mentioned individually you felt like you could be fired at any moment, but what
嗯，你们提到过个人感觉随时都可能被解雇，但对于

1277
00:42:15.700 --> 00:42:16.800
about the show as a whole?
整部剧来说呢？

1278
00:42:16.860 --> 00:42:18.800
Yeah, we always felt like we were pretty much on the bubble.
是啊，我们一直觉得我们基本处于被砍的边缘。

1279
00:42:18.820 --> 00:42:20.080
We never, ever...
我们从来，从来没有……

1280
00:42:20.080 --> 00:42:21.380
Maybe three to four or four to five.
可能也就三到四季，或者四到五季的时候。

1281
00:42:21.500 --> 00:42:23.460
Maybe one season we knew were picked up for the next one.
可能只有一季我们知道自己续订了下一季。

1282
00:42:23.540 --> 00:42:24.140
Maybe we were kind of...
也许我们当时有点……

1283
00:42:24.140 --> 00:42:26.640
It was also just a weird position to be a kid's show.
作为一部儿童剧，我们的处境也很奇怪。

1284
00:42:26.940 --> 00:42:28.460
We felt like nobody was watching.
我们觉得根本没人看。

1285
00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:31.340
You know, like, we'd had no cultural feedback.
你知道，就像我们没有任何文化反馈一样。

1286
00:42:31.700 --> 00:42:31.920
Yeah.
是啊。

1287
00:42:31.920 --> 00:42:32.760
Like, there was no...
就像，根本没有……

1288
00:42:32.760 --> 00:42:33.820
There was no online culture.
当时根本没有网络文化。

1289
00:42:34.160 --> 00:42:34.220
Right.
没错。

1290
00:42:34.300 --> 00:42:36.640
But there was also just no way that kids could...
但同时，孩子们也根本没法……

1291
00:42:36.640 --> 00:42:39.240
Like, we would get recognized, like, couldn't go to the mall.
我们会被认出来，比如，没法去商场。

1292
00:42:39.380 --> 00:42:39.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1293
00:42:39.620 --> 00:42:43.380
But otherwise, like, as far as, like, the industry, we were nothing.
但除此之外，在业内看来，我们什么都不是。

1294
00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:45.580
We felt like we were getting no...
我们觉得我们没得到任何……

1295
00:42:45.580 --> 00:42:48.640
You know, and so it's only now that we're like, oh my God, we were big.
你知道，所以直到现在我们才意识到，天哪，原来我们当时那么火。

1296
00:42:48.700 --> 00:42:51.900
Well, we also had one of our other executive producers on, not the one who used to give
嗯，我们之前请过另一位执行制片人，不是以前给我们提意见的那位，

1297
00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:55.220
us notes, but another one who just recently came on and said, that was also a network
而是最近才加入的那位，他说这也是电视网的

1298
00:42:55.220 --> 00:42:58.340
thing where they specifically didn't want you to know that you were
手段，他们特意不想让你们知道自己

1299
00:42:58.340 --> 00:43:02.360
popular so that they couldn't go and ask for more money to make more, make the show.
很受欢迎，这样你们就不会去要求加薪来制作更多的剧集了。

1300
00:43:02.480 --> 00:43:02.530
Right.
没错。

1301
00:43:02.530 --> 00:43:03.940
They wanted us to feel like we were lucky to be there.
他们想让我们觉得能待在那里是我们的幸运。

1302
00:43:03.940 --> 00:43:06.800
So they would, if you're always on the bubble, then you're lucky we're giving you this budget.
所以他们会说，如果你一直处于被砍的边缘，那我们给你这笔预算你就该感到幸运了。

1303
00:43:07.160 --> 00:43:10.220
Like, so don't ask for any more because you barely got picked up.
就像是，别再要求更多了，因为你们能被续订已经是勉强了。

1304
00:43:10.420 --> 00:43:14.680
Where if we knew the show was, or they knew that the show was popular, the executive producers
而如果我们知道节目，或者他们知道节目很受欢迎，执行制片人就会

1305
00:43:14.680 --> 00:43:15.940
go in and ask for the moon.
去争取最好的待遇。

1306
00:43:15.940 --> 00:43:19.960
And so to stop that, they would kind of make us seem like we're just, we're lucky to be
为了阻止这种情况，他们会让我们觉得我们只是，能待在那里是我们的幸运。

1307
00:43:19.960 --> 00:43:20.080
there.
待在那里。

1308
00:43:20.160 --> 00:43:21.120
Don't forget you're lucky to be there.
别忘了，你能待在那里是你的幸运。

1309
00:43:21.260 --> 00:43:24.420
Also, we were canceled in 2000 with what, like a 25 share?
而且，我们在2000年被砍的时候，收视份额大概有25吧？

1310
00:43:24.680 --> 00:43:25.080
Yeah, right.
是啊，没错。

1311
00:43:25.240 --> 00:43:28.900
And like, you know, nowadays, everybody would chill for that kind of audience.
而且，你知道，放到现在，所有人都会为那样的收视率感到高兴。

1312
00:43:28.900 --> 00:43:29.120
Yeah, yes.
是啊，没错。

1313
00:43:29.300 --> 00:43:30.660
But that was a big drop for us.
但对我们来说，那是一个很大的跌幅。

1314
00:43:30.880 --> 00:43:33.200
So that was, I mean, it was like, oh my God, we're only getting a 25.
所以当时的感觉就是，天哪，我们竟然只有25的份额。

1315
00:43:33.460 --> 00:43:33.820
Yeah, we're done.
完了，我们要结束了。

1316
00:43:33.820 --> 00:43:37.320
Did you feel like you got to wrap up the show?
你觉得你们有机会为剧集画上句号吗？

1317
00:43:37.760 --> 00:43:38.520
Yeah, yeah.
有，有的。

1318
00:43:38.720 --> 00:43:38.860
Definitely.
绝对有。

1319
00:43:38.860 --> 00:43:43.780
We got a nice, you know, we had a very nice hour long with the retrospective and where
我们做得很棒，你知道，我们有一个非常好的长达一小时的回顾特辑，还有

1320
00:43:43.780 --> 00:43:44.420
everybody moves.
大家各自的去向。

1321
00:43:44.480 --> 00:43:46.240
We really did get a chance to say goodbye.
我们确实有机会好好告别。

1322
00:43:46.420 --> 00:43:47.280
It wasn't like we were just done.
并不是说结束就直接结束了。

1323
00:43:47.280 --> 00:43:48.600
And our final scene was so great.
而且我们最后的场景太棒了。

1324
00:43:48.840 --> 00:43:50.460
It was a really nice final scene.
那是一个非常美好的结局场景。

1325
00:43:50.540 --> 00:43:51.580
And we were all like really crying.
我们当时都真的在哭。

1326
00:43:51.840 --> 00:43:52.640
Actually, in the classroom.
就在教室里。

1327
00:43:52.640 --> 00:43:54.040
We didn't rehearse it throughout the week.
我们那一周都没有排练过。

1328
00:43:54.140 --> 00:43:57.500
We just read it at table read and then shot it once in front of the audience.
我们只是在剧本围读时读了一遍，然后在观众面前拍了一次。

1329
00:43:57.660 --> 00:43:58.060
That was it.
就这样。

1330
00:43:58.080 --> 00:44:03.600
And so it's us saying goodbye to Bill Daniels as Mr. Feeney and all of us just real emotion.
所以那是我们向饰演费尼先生的比尔·丹尼尔斯告别，我们所有人的情绪都是真实的。

1331
00:44:04.520 --> 00:44:06.820
Brian kind of talking to each other in character.
布莱恩在角色状态中互相交谈。

1332
00:44:07.340 --> 00:44:08.100
Very emotional.
非常感人。

1333
00:44:08.300 --> 00:44:08.700
Wow.
哇。

1334
00:44:08.880 --> 00:44:10.220
I'm very thankful for that.
我对此非常感激。

1335
00:44:10.280 --> 00:44:13.420
And I don't think a lot of, you know, actors get that experience.
而且我不认为很多演员能有那样的经历。

1336
00:44:13.600 --> 00:44:15.100
It's just you're just done.
通常就是直接结束了。

1337
00:44:15.300 --> 00:44:17.040
You don't get any like notice.
你不会得到任何通知。

1338
00:44:17.260 --> 00:44:18.740
But yeah, your character doesn't get closure.
而且，你的角色也得不到结局。

1339
00:44:18.940 --> 00:44:21.120
You don't get closure as a group or as a crew.
你作为团队或剧组也得不到一个圆满的告别。

1340
00:44:21.440 --> 00:44:23.560
A lot of people just get canceled.
很多人就是直接被砍了。

1341
00:44:23.720 --> 00:44:25.200
You're just like, not next year, guys.
就像是，伙计们，明年没戏了。

1342
00:44:25.380 --> 00:44:26.080
You're like, oh.
你会觉得，哦。

1343
00:44:26.520 --> 00:44:30.100
For me, moving into any other acting job after Boy Meets World was a shock.
对我来说，在《男孩成长记》之后去接任何其他演艺工作都是一种冲击。

1344
00:44:30.240 --> 00:44:31.700
It was like, wait, we're not all best friends.
就像是，等等，我们不是所有人都是最好的朋友吗？

1345
00:44:31.700 --> 00:44:33.160
We're going to be together forever.
我们不是要永远在一起吗？

1346
00:44:33.160 --> 00:44:34.600
You're like, oh, right.
你会意识到，哦，原来不是。

1347
00:44:34.680 --> 00:44:36.340
That is such a rare gift.
那真是一份罕见的礼物。

1348
00:44:36.640 --> 00:44:36.780
Yeah.
是啊。

1349
00:44:37.260 --> 00:44:41.520
Well, I was going to say that I think that's something that our casts have in common, which
嗯，我想说的是，我认为这是我们剧组共同拥有的东西，那就是

1350
00:44:41.520 --> 00:44:45.840
is that, like Angela was saying, for a lot of the people in the office, this was really
就像安吉拉刚才说的，对于办公室里的很多人来说，这真的是

1351
00:44:45.840 --> 00:44:47.400
our first big job.
我们第一份大工作。

1352
00:44:47.660 --> 00:44:47.880
Yeah.
没错。

1353
00:44:47.880 --> 00:44:51.680
And you're a very open vessel when it's your first big job.
当你第一次接大活儿时，你就像个毫无防备的容器。

1354
00:44:51.700 --> 00:44:54.200
And we all like learned together.
我们当时都是一起学习的。

1355
00:44:54.200 --> 00:44:56.780
We learned about parts of the industry together.
我们一起了解了这个行业的方方面面。

1356
00:44:57.040 --> 00:44:58.960
Like none of us had ever done a junket.
比如我们谁都没参加过媒体见面会。

1357
00:44:59.380 --> 00:45:01.380
None of us had ever been to the upfront.
我们谁都没参加过新剧推介会。

1358
00:45:01.560 --> 00:45:06.260
So to all the like business stuff that goes behind the making of a show or the publicity
所以对于所有那些节目制作背后的商业运作或宣传工作，

1359
00:45:06.260 --> 00:45:06.860
or anything.
或者其他任何事情。

1360
00:45:06.860 --> 00:45:10.740
And so we're really bonded, not just because of the show we were on, but because we kind
所以我们真的建立了深厚的感情，不仅是因为我们合作的那部剧，还因为我们算是

1361
00:45:10.740 --> 00:45:13.160
of learned about the entertainment business together.
一起摸索着了解了娱乐圈。

1362
00:45:13.400 --> 00:45:13.820
Satellite Mediator.
卫星连线采访。

1363
00:45:14.160 --> 00:45:14.420
Yeah.
没错。

1364
00:45:15.160 --> 00:45:16.200
Get up at 4 a.m.
凌晨四点起床。

1365
00:45:16.360 --> 00:45:17.900
and talk to 25 news stations.
然后接受25家新闻台的采访。

1366
00:45:18.320 --> 00:45:19.540
25 radio stations.
25家广播电台。

1367
